      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/microglanis-carlae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Usually the \"typical\" catfish with long barbels become quite big and are therefore also called \"predatory catfish\" in the hobby. However, there is a species from South America, more precisely from Paraguay, which is also suitable for nano aquariums, since so far no specimens larger than about 4 cm have been known from the wild: Microglanis carlae. With about 2.5 cm length (without tail fin) the little animals are already sexually mature.</p>"
